# The sandbox always bind-mounts the live tests/ tree read-only over
# C:\app\tests (scripts/sandbox/docker_sandbox.py). Baking a second copy in
# via `COPY . ./` leaves an image-layer directory underneath that mount, and
# pytest then builds the tests package tree twice, collecting every test node
# under a duplicate nodeid. No build stage reads tests/, so keep it out of the
# build context entirely and let the mount be the only copy.
tests/
